#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# multiply_sides

#% text
# `multiply_sides(rel, c)` multiplies every side of the equation or inequality rel by c.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# An inequality is reversed for a negative c. When the sign of c is not decided the result is a piecewise over c > 0 and c < 0 (over c != 0 for an equation), with rel itself otherwise.

#% item
# `assumptions:` facts that decide the sign of c. `multiply_sides(a == b, c == d)` multiplies side by side.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
multiply_sides(x/2 == 3, 2)
#% output
#= x == 6

#% cell
multiply_sides(x > 1, -2)
#% output
#= -2*x < -2

#% cell
multiply_sides(x/a > 1, a, assumptions: a > 0)
#% output
#= x > a

#% cell
multiply_sides(a == b, c)
#% output
#= piecewise([[a*c == b*c, c != 0]], a == b)

#% section
# See also

#% text
